IMPORT prelude

-- Retrenchment benefit under the Tripartite Advisory on Managing Excess Manpower and Responsible Retrenchment (TAMEM), and
-- the Workfare Income Supplement (WIS) for employees -- AS PUBLISHED by the Ministry of Manpower, the Tripartite Alliance and
-- the CPF Board. AS PUBLISHED, NOT LAW.
--
-- SOURCES, all read on 12 October 2026:
--   (1) MOM, "Responsible retrenchment" (last updated 14 July 2026):
--       https://www.mom.gov.sg/employment-practices/retrenchment/responsible-retrenchment
--   (2) MOM FAQs (each last updated 14 March 2024):
--       https://www.mom.gov.sg/faq/retrenchment/can-my-company-terminate-my-employment-contract-without-paying-any-rb-and-if-employers-must-pay-rb
--       https://www.mom.gov.sg/faq/retrenchment/are-employees-who-have-worked-less-than-2-years-entitled-to-retrenchment-benefit
--       https://www.mom.gov.sg/faq/retrenchment/are-my-employees-who-are-aged-63-or-above-eligible-for-retrenchment-benefit-or-eap
--   (3) the Advisory itself, "(Updated 20 January 2023)", Annex C part II:
--       https://www.mom.gov.sg/-/media/mom/documents/employment-practices/guidelines/tripartite-advisory-on-managing-excess-manpower-and-responsible-retrenchment.pdf
--   (4) TADM FAQ "I have been retrenched" (last updated 2 March 2026): https://www.tal.sg/tadm/faqs/advisory/i-have-been-retrenched
--   (5) CPF Board, "Workfare Income Supplement" (last updated 18 June 2026; tables for Work Years 2024 and 2025):
--       https://www.cpf.gov.sg/member/growing-your-savings/government-support/workfare-income-supplement
--   (6) CPF Board, WIS eligibility criteria (last updated 23 July 2026):
--       https://www.cpf.gov.sg/service/article/what-are-the-eligibility-criteria-of-the-workfare-income-supplement-scheme
--   (7) CPF Board, WIS employee calculator for Work Year 2026 (last updated 3 August 2026):
--       https://www.cpf.gov.sg/member/tools-and-services/calculators/workfare-income-supplement-employee-work-year-2026-calculator
--
-- AS PUBLISHED, NOT LAW. Neither scheme is a rule of law in the form encoded here. MOM says retrenchment benefit is "not
-- mandated by law"; TADM says that under the Employment Act it "is not compulsory". The Advisory is a tripartite guideline
-- (MOM, NTUC, SNEF); its norm is a range for negotiation, not a sum anyone can claim. WIS figures are set by the Government
-- and change by announcement, without amending any Act. Every figure below carries the date of the page it came from, and
-- may already be out of date on the day it is read. Where a page refers to an Act (the Employment Act for retrenchment
-- notifications and the TADM statement; the CPF Act, implicitly, for WIS paid into CPF accounts) the statutory test is left
-- to that Act's row (subjects/sg/employment-act-1968, subjects/sg/central-provident-fund-act-1953).
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0276 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl (cradle-to-grave-jun-hao, event j087,
-- 30 November 2055: Jun Hao, a security officer of 21 years' service earning $3,100 a month, is retrenched at 49). The
-- scenario date is 2055; this encoding answers on the policy as published in October 2026.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the WIS amount for a given income (the pages give only the yearly maximum for each age band, not how the
-- payout varies with income -- so no monthly sum is computed for an eligible worker); WIS for self-employed persons beyond
-- their yearly maximum, and for platform workers; the self-employed MediSave conditions; how a 12-month average counts
-- months without income (an input here); the levels of concessionary WIS; WIS for Work Years before 2024 (the pages read
-- give the property limit for 2023 only); the Workfare Skills Support scheme; the Advisory's selection criteria, notice and
-- notification duties, and its ex-gratia payment (no amount given); the Employee Assistance Payment for those 63 and over
-- (named, not quantified, on the MOM FAQ; it lives in the Tripartite Guidelines for Re-employment of Older Workers).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. One pass from the pages, written with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Retrenchment benefit -- the Tripartite Advisory (Annex C part II, updated 20 January 2023), as MOM publishes it`

-- MOM FAQ (14 March 2024): retrenchment benefit is "not mandated by law". TADM (2 March 2026) says the same of the
-- Employment Act. So the legal entitlement the ledger assumes is not what the publisher says; see NOTES.md finding 1.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`retrenchment benefit is mandated by law, as MOM publishes it` MEANS FALSE

-- Annex C II(i)(a): "Employees with 2 years' service or more are eligible". Fewer than 2 years: an ex-gratia payment
-- "could be granted" (not encoded: no amount).
GIVEN `years of service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for retrenchment benefit under the Advisory` `years of service` IF
    `years of service` AT LEAST 2

-- Annex C II(iii)(a): if retrenchment follows "shortly after" a salary cut, the salary before the cut is used. Whether it
-- followed shortly after is an input.
GIVEN `current monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `monthly salary before the cut` IS A NUMBER, `follows shortly after a salary cut` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the salary to compute retrenchment benefit on` `current monthly salary` `monthly salary before the cut` `follows shortly after a salary cut` MEANS
    IF `follows shortly after a salary cut`
    THEN `monthly salary before the cut`
    ELSE `current monthly salary`

-- Annex C II(ii)(b): the prevailing norm is between "2 weeks to one month salary per year of service", depending on the
-- company's financial position and the industry norm. The Advisory does not say how two weeks' salary is reckoned from a
-- monthly salary. NAIVE READING: half a month's salary. The alternative (12 months' pay over 26 fortnights) is given below
-- and compared in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `monthly salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`two weeks' salary, read as half a month` `monthly salary` MEANS
    `monthly salary` TIMES 0.5

GIVEN `monthly salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`two weeks' salary, reckoned as a twenty-sixth of a year's pay` `monthly salary` MEANS
    `monthly salary` TIMES 12 DIVIDED BY 26

-- The bottom of the norm: two weeks' salary (read as half a month) for each year of service; nil if not eligible.
GIVEN `monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `years of service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bottom of the Advisory's norm` `monthly salary` `years of service` MEANS
    IF `eligible for retrenchment benefit under the Advisory` `years of service`
    THEN `two weeks' salary, read as half a month` `monthly salary` TIMES `years of service`
    ELSE 0

-- The top of the norm: one month's salary for each year of service; nil if not eligible.
GIVEN `monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `years of service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the top of the Advisory's norm` `monthly salary` `years of service` MEANS
    IF `eligible for retrenchment benefit under the Advisory` `years of service`
    THEN `monthly salary` TIMES `years of service`
    ELSE 0

-- Annex C II(ii)(a) and (b): the quantum is first what the collective agreement or contract provides (an input here);
-- where the collective agreement of a unionised company stipulates it, "the norm is one month salary for each year of
-- service". This gives the single figure the Advisory names in that case, and otherwise the top of the range.
GIVEN `monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `years of service` IS A NUMBER, `unionised and the collective agreement stipulates the quantum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Advisory's norm where a collective agreement stipulates the quantum` `monthly salary` `years of service` `unionised and the collective agreement stipulates the quantum` MEANS
    IF `unionised and the collective agreement stipulates the quantum`
    THEN `the top of the Advisory's norm` `monthly salary` `years of service`
    ELSE 0

-- Whether a proposed sum lies within the Advisory's norm (bottom read as half a month per year).
GIVEN `sum offered` IS A NUMBER, `monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `years of service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sum is within the Advisory's norm` `sum offered` `monthly salary` `years of service` IF
        `eligible for retrenchment benefit under the Advisory` `years of service`
    AND `sum offered` AT LEAST `the bottom of the Advisory's norm` `monthly salary` `years of service`
    AND `sum offered` AT MOST `the top of the Advisory's norm` `monthly salary` `years of service`

-- MOM FAQ (14 March 2024): for employees aged 63 or above an employer can use the Employee Assistance Payment recommended
-- in the Tripartite Guidelines for Re-employment of Older Workers, unless the collective agreement or contract provides a
-- retrenchment benefit.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, `contract or collective agreement provides retrenchment benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer may use the Employee Assistance Payment instead` age `contract or collective agreement provides retrenchment benefit` IF
        age AT LEAST 63
    AND (NOT `contract or collective agreement provides retrenchment benefit`)

-- MOM "Responsible retrenchment" (14 July 2026): neither employee nor employer pays CPF contributions on retrenchment
-- benefit.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CPF contributions are payable on retrenchment benefit` MEANS FALSE

-- TADM (2 March 2026): a claim for retrenchment benefit not paid according to the contract or collective agreement is to
-- be filed "within 6 months from the last date of employment".
GIVEN `months since the last date of employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a TADM claim is in time` `months since the last date of employment` IF
    `months since the last date of employment` AT MOST 6

§ `Workfare Income Supplement for employees, as the CPF Board publishes it`

DECLARE Worker HAS
    `Singapore Citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age at 31 December of the work year` IS A NUMBER
    `person with disabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ComCare Short-to-Medium-Term Assistance recipient or qualifying caregiver` IS A BOOLEAN
    `worked as an employee in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gross income for the month` IS A NUMBER
    `average gross monthly income over the past 12 months` IS A NUMBER
    `annual value of home at 31 December of the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
    `properties owned, with spouse if married` IS A NUMBER
    married IS A BOOLEAN
    `spouse's assessable income for the preceding Year of Assessment` IS A NUMBER

-- The pages read give the income cap for Work Years 2024 and 2025, and the Work Year 2026 calculator repeats the 2025 cap.
-- Nothing earlier is encoded.
GIVEN `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pages read give WIS figures for` `work year` IF
    `work year` AT LEAST 2024

-- Income cap per month and for the 12-month average: $3,000 from Work Year 2025 (the CPF page, 18 June 2026; repeated by
-- the Work Year 2026 calculator, 3 August 2026); $2,500 for Work Year 2024. Later years: AS PUBLISHED IN OCTOBER 2026, the
-- 2025 figure, until changed.
GIVEN `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the WIS income cap` `work year` MEANS
    IF `work year` AT LEAST 2025 THEN 3000 ELSE 2500

-- The income floor: $500 a month, waived for the concessionary groups.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the WIS income floor` MEANS 500

-- Home annual value limit, assessed as at 31 December of the preceding year: $21,000 from Work Year 2024; $13,000 for
-- Work Year 2023 (eligibility page, 23 July 2026).
GIVEN `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the WIS annual value limit` `work year` MEANS
    IF `work year` AT LEAST 2024 THEN 21000 ELSE 13000

GIVEN w IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the WIS age condition` w IF
        w's `age at 31 December of the work year` AT LEAST 30
    OR  w's `person with disabilities`

GIVEN w IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in a WIS concessionary group` w IF
        w's `person with disabilities`
    OR  w's `ComCare Short-to-Medium-Term Assistance recipient or qualifying caregiver`

-- Employees: gross income for the month worked between $500 and the cap (the floor waived for concessionary groups), and
-- an average over the past 12 months not above the cap. WIS is paid "for every month that you work" (calculator): a month
-- without work as an employee earns nothing.
GIVEN w IS A Worker, `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the WIS income condition for the month` w `work year` IF
        w's `worked as an employee in the month`
    AND w's `gross income for the month` GREATER THAN 0
    AND w's `gross income for the month` AT MOST `the WIS income cap` `work year`
    AND (    w's `gross income for the month` AT LEAST `the WIS income floor`
         OR  `in a WIS concessionary group` w)
    AND w's `average gross monthly income over the past 12 months` AT MOST `the WIS income cap` `work year`

GIVEN w IS A Worker, `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the WIS property condition` w `work year` IF
        w's `annual value of home at 31 December of the preceding year` AT MOST `the WIS annual value limit` `work year`
    AND w's `properties owned, with spouse if married` AT MOST 1

GIVEN w IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the WIS spouse condition` w IF
        (NOT w's married)
    OR  w's `spouse's assessable income for the preceding Year of Assessment` AT MOST 70000

GIVEN w IS A Worker, `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies for employee WIS for the month` w `work year` IF
        `the pages read give WIS figures for` `work year`
    AND w's `Singapore Citizen`
    AND `meets the WIS age condition` w
    AND `meets the WIS income condition for the month` w `work year`
    AND `meets the WIS property condition` w `work year`
    AND `meets the WIS spouse condition` w

-- The age band used for the payout: persons with disabilities get the 60-and-above amount (CPF page).
GIVEN w IS A Worker
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age for the WIS payout` w MEANS
    IF w's `person with disabilities`
    THEN 60
    ELSE w's `age at 31 December of the work year`

-- Maximum WIS per year for an employee (CPF page, 18 June 2026). WY2025: 30-34 $2,450; 35-44 $3,500; 45-59 $4,200; 60 and
-- above $4,900. WY2024: $2,100; $3,000; $3,600; $4,200. The pages read show no table for 2026; from 2025 on the 2025 table
-- is used, AS PUBLISHED IN OCTOBER 2026.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum yearly employee WIS for the age` age `work year` MEANS
    IF age LESS THAN 30 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `work year` AT LEAST 2025
         THEN IF age AT MOST 34 THEN 2450
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 44 THEN 3500
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 59 THEN 4200
                        ELSE 4900
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 34 THEN 2100
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 44 THEN 3000
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 59 THEN 3600
                        ELSE 4200

GIVEN w IS A Worker, `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum yearly employee WIS` w `work year` MEANS
    `the maximum yearly employee WIS for the age` (`the age for the WIS payout` w) `work year`

-- Maximum WIS per year for a self-employed person (CPF page). WY2025: $1,633; $2,333; $2,800; $3,267. WY2024: $1,400;
-- $2,000; $2,400; $2,800.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum yearly self-employed WIS for the age` age `work year` MEANS
    IF age LESS THAN 30 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `work year` AT LEAST 2025
         THEN IF age AT MOST 34 THEN 1633
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 44 THEN 2333
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 59 THEN 2800
                        ELSE 3267
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 34 THEN 1400
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 44 THEN 2000
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 59 THEN 2400
                        ELSE 2800

-- Employees: "40% of your WIS in cash and 60% in CPF contributions" (CPF page).
GIVEN `wis amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cash part of employee WIS` `wis amount` MEANS
    `wis amount` TIMES 0.4

GIVEN `wis amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the CPF part of employee WIS` `wis amount` MEANS
    `wis amount` TIMES 0.6

-- Self-employed persons: 10% cash, 90% MediSave.
GIVEN `wis amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cash part of self-employed WIS` `wis amount` MEANS
    `wis amount` TIMES 0.1

-- Employees are paid monthly: work in month x is paid to a bank or PayNow account by the end of month x+2 (CPF page).
-- Months are numbered 1 to 12; the result is the month number, with the year carried below.
GIVEN `work month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month WIS for the work month is paid by` `work month` MEANS
    IF `work month` AT MOST 10
    THEN `work month` PLUS 2
    ELSE `work month` MINUS 10

GIVEN `work month` IS A NUMBER, `work year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year WIS for the work month is paid by` `work month` `work year` MEANS
    IF `work month` AT MOST 10
    THEN `work year`
    ELSE `work year` PLUS 1
